========================================================================
  ROOT SPACE ANGLES AND TOURNAMENT STRUCTURE
  opus-2026-03-22-S158
========================================================================

PART 1: THE A_{n-1} ROOT SYSTEM ANGLES
------------------------------------------------------------

  In the A_{n-1} root system, the positive roots are:
    α_{ij} = e_i - e_j  for i < j

  These are the ARCS of a tournament: arc (i→j) = root e_i - e_j.

  The inner product of two roots:
    <α_{ij}, α_{kl}> = δ_{ik} + δ_{jl} - δ_{il} - δ_{jk}

  This takes values in {-2, -1, 0, +1, +2}.
  The ANGLE θ between the roots (|α| = √2 for all roots):
    cos(θ) = <α,β> / (|α||β|) = <α,β> / 2

  INNER PRODUCT → ANGLE → GEOMETRIC MEANING:

   <α,β>    cos(θ)         θ  meaning                                 
  ──────  ────────  ────────  ────────────────────────────────────────
      +2    +1.000      0.0°  same arc (i=k, j=l)
      +1    +0.500     60.0°  share one vertex, SAME role (both start or both end)
      +0    +0.000     90.0°  completely disjoint (no shared vertex)
      -1    -0.500    120.0°  share one vertex, OPPOSITE roles
      -2    -1.000    180.0°  opposite arc (i=l, j=k, reversed)


